config.hosts:
Color per SSH host (name as in `~/.ssh/config`, wildcards `*` and `?` allowed). The value can be a color, or an object with its own areas and label. Use `wsl:<distro>`, `container:<name>`, `codespace:<name>`, `tunnel:<name>` or `folder:<path>` for other environments and project folders; a folder entry wins over its environment.

```json
{
  "prod-*": "#c0392b",
  "dev": { "color": "#27ae60", "elements": ["statusBar"], "label": "DEV" }
}
```

The easiest way: the **Host Colors: Open Manager** command.
